  "title": "Cloudflare released a model that only makes decisions",
  "narration": "Cloudflare released Clef, a 27-billion-parameter multimodal decision model. It does not write essays, poems, or apology paragraphs. Instead, Clef scores the allowed answers you provide. Input can be text, JSON, images, or video. Output is a probability for every permitted option. That makes it useful for classification and agent decisions. There is no free-form generation to parse afterward. Clef is post-trained from Qwen 3.8 27B. Cloudflare released it under Apache 2.0. The model is also available through Workers AI. Sometimes you need a decision, not another paragraph. The cure for chatbot verbosity is removing the chatbot part.",
